  "question": {
    "text": "Two simple harmonic motions are represented by the equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math> The amplitude of the second motion is _____ times the amplitude in the first motion.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>[</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p>",
